# Enforced Regression Guards

These tests mechanically enforce security boundaries. When one fails, confirm the underlying change
is an intentional, reviewed security decision before touching the test.

## Forbidden-pattern guard

`test/unit/security/forbidden_rails_patterns_test.rb` enforces:

- No test-framework detection or known test-only bypass in `app/` or `lib/` (for example
  `defined?(Minitest)`, `defined?(RSpec)`, `ENV["RAILS_ENV"]`, `TEST_VERIFICATION_COOKIE_PREFIX`).
  See `no-test-only-code`.
- `skip_before_action :enforce_verification_if_required`, `:enforce_step_up_prereqs!`, and
  `:authenticate_client!` may appear only in the reviewed `SENSITIVE_SKIP_ALLOWLIST`. Adding a new
  file that skips one of these fails the suite until the boundary change is reviewed.

## RI routing contract guard

`test/unit/security/ri_routing_contract_test.rb` pins the region (`ri`) request-context contract:

- every `<family>/<edition>` controller directory is classified as participating or exempt,
- every participating surface `ApplicationController` includes `PreferenceGlobal` and registers
  `before_action :set_region`,
- the set of controllers skipping `set_region` equals `RI_SKIP_ALLOWLIST` exactly.

Skipping `set_region` on a controller that renders regional HTML removes `ri` from every URL it
generates, because `default_url_options` propagates the region from the request params only. Treat
an allowlist edit as a reviewed boundary change. See
`plans/analysis/ri-preference-routing-regression-audit.md`.

## Bare controller guard

`test/controllers/apex/app/bare_controller_test.rb` pins the set of controllers inheriting
`Apex::App::BareController` (a no-op `public_strict!` boundary). A new descendant fails the suite
until it is confirmed to be a public, self-defending endpoint. See `controller-inheritance`.

## On failure

Do not just edit the allowlist or the pinned set to make the suite green. Confirm first that the
change is a deliberate, reviewed security decision; the failing test is the review gate, not an
obstacle.
